And in AI, Europe is losing on scale.

01:01:37.180 --> 01:01:42.380
There is no point pretending otherwise, but it retains the ability to absorb innovation

01:01:42.380 --> 01:01:45.780
which is what ultimately matters for preserving productivity.

01:01:45.780 --> 01:01:52.020
It is building its own AI companies and it still controls several critical choke points.

01:01:52.020 --> 01:01:56.840
Perhaps this is where we finally can stop to answer the question posed at the very beginning

01:01:56.840 --> 01:01:58.600
of this episode.

01:01:58.600 --> 01:02:00.260
Is Europe declining?

01:02:00.260 --> 01:02:01.580
No.

01:02:01.580 --> 01:02:02.780
Europe has problems.

01:02:02.780 --> 01:02:04.620
At times, very serious ones.

01:02:04.620 --> 01:02:07.580
It is slow, politically fragmented and aging.

01:02:07.580 --> 01:02:09.540
It scales capital more slowly.

01:02:09.540 --> 01:02:13.940
It is not the technological frontier to the same extent as America.

01:02:13.940 --> 01:02:18.220
But having problems is not the same thing as being in decline.

01:02:18.220 --> 01:02:23.220
We are still talking about one of the wealthiest, most productive and most attractive places

01:02:23.220 --> 01:02:25.060
to live on the planet.

01:02:25.060 --> 01:02:30.560
About an economy with an enormous market, advanced industrial base, capital, expertise and

01:02:30.560 --> 01:02:35.320
technological choke points that other powers need as well.

01:02:35.320 --> 01:02:36.820
Everyone has problems.

01:02:36.820 --> 01:02:40.320
Compared with Russia's, Europe's problems are almost trivial.

01:02:40.320 --> 01:02:41.320
China?

01:02:41.320 --> 01:02:45.960
Yes, it has recorded extraordinary successes over the past decades.

01:02:45.960 --> 01:02:49.000
But is it a civilization flowing with milk and honey?

01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:50.320
Absolutely not.

01:02:50.320 --> 01:02:55.120
The Chinese Communist Party relies on a wide range of coercive tools presciently because the

01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:59.880
country faces serious problems at both the micro and macro level.

01:02:59.880 --> 01:03:05.560
We discussed them two years ago and by now that story probably deserves an update.

01:03:05.560 --> 01:03:10.520
Nor can we say that America has reached its end of history, quite the opposite.

01:03:10.520 --> 01:03:15.320
Many Americans today look at the condition of their own country with disappointment, even

01:03:15.320 --> 01:03:20.960
resignation despite its dominance according to many conventional metrics.

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:26.120
None of this changes the fact that Europe needs another major round of adaptation, and it

01:03:26.120 --> 01:03:31.200
It certainly does not mean that sounding the alarm bell over its weaknesses is somehow

01:03:31.200 --> 01:03:32.200
misguided.

01:03:32.200 --> 01:03:34.040
Quite the opposite.

01:03:34.040 --> 01:03:38.440
Identifying problems and creating pressure to solve them are natural features of any

01:03:38.440 --> 01:03:41.520
system capable of adapting.

01:03:41.520 --> 01:03:46.040
Freedom of speech, one of the foundations of the European model, unlike the Russian or

01:03:46.040 --> 01:03:51.040
Chinese models, allows virtually any narrative to circulate freely.

01:03:51.040 --> 01:03:55.320
The narrative of European decline is popular and is frequently amplified.

01:03:55.320 --> 01:04:00.200
among other places in China and Russia, while those same states often suppress negative

01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:03.480
reporting about their own internal condition.

01:04:03.480 --> 01:04:08.080
On the other hand, this freedom is enormously valuable because it serves as a kind of

01:04:08.080 --> 01:04:09.800
self-correction mechanism.

01:04:09.800 --> 01:04:15.040
When something is broken, we will almost certainly hear about it, and that creates social pressure

01:04:15.040 --> 01:04:16.920
to fix it.

01:04:16.920 --> 01:04:20.960
But the same openness can also be turned against a system that provides it.

01:04:20.960 --> 01:04:26.160
You can convince its citizens that their social model and their future are heading toward

01:04:26.160 --> 01:04:32.480
collapse, and that everything Europe does is too late, too weak, or simply wrong.

01:04:32.480 --> 01:04:36.880
But Europe is making the adaptive effort I have been talking about, yet often with all

01:04:36.880 --> 01:04:41.280
the sluggishness built into its political landscape, but it is adapting.

01:04:41.280 --> 01:04:47.400
And according to the basic logic of evolution, that process never really ends.

01:04:47.400 --> 01:04:52.680
I think it is that the very same sluggishness we criticize so often does not produce only

01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:54.560
weaknesses.

01:04:54.560 --> 01:04:59.320
In a world where the rules can change faster than anyone can calculate the second and

01:04:59.320 --> 01:05:05.040
third order consequences, moving slowly is no longer purely at disadvantage.

01:05:05.040 --> 01:05:11.320
Europe is less vulnerable to violent swings precisely because it is difficult to swing violently.

01:05:11.320 --> 01:05:14.760
Even if that quote lunatic takes power in one country.

01:05:14.760 --> 01:05:21.040
The rest of the system has enough weight and enough time to absorb and balance that influence.

01:05:21.040 --> 01:05:24.240
And that brings us back to where we started.

01:05:24.240 --> 01:05:28.840
Capital is returning to European markets partly because valuations are lower.

01:05:28.840 --> 01:05:34.880
Of course, but Europe also possesses another asset today, one whose value rises with every

01:05:34.880 --> 01:05:38.640
new dose of chaos in the world around it.

01:05:38.640 --> 01:05:39.640
Predectability.

01:05:39.640 --> 01:05:44.720
Atari is unlikely to change here on Wednesday morning because of a social media post.

01:05:44.720 --> 01:05:47.520
Sounds boring? Perhaps.

01:05:47.520 --> 01:05:52.120
But predictability has become a scarce commodity in today's world.

01:05:52.120 --> 01:05:56.120
And that is one thing Europe happens to produce in abundance.
